": 21, "text": "D6 lost 19.1 points, taking the lead from -24.9 to -44.0. The engine wanted D7, the point White took next. The board before this move shows the Black centre stones pressed against White's wall, and by move 33 White had captured six stones."}, {"turn": 34, "text": "The 14k's H3 was its worst move, losing 28.3 points and bringing the lead from -84.2 back to -55.9. The engine's choice was H6. It was a rare chance for Black, but the game was still far out of reach."}, {"turn": 35, "text": "Opus 5.5 did not use the gift. H2 lost 26.7 points and sent the lead from -55.9 to -82.6, while the engine's choice was H6. Opus 5.5 played H6 two turns later, when it was worth -0.2 and the lead was -83.1."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py parses a pasted board and prints each group's stones and liberties, flagging groups with two or fewer liberties, and count.py flood-fills empty regions to tally territory and stones with named dead stones removed. Both only analyze the current position, never generate, score or rank candidate moves, and never look ahead.", "stop": false}}